# Keeps the build context small/fast. The Dockerfile only COPYs cwatm/,
# src/, cwatm_model.py and requirements_docker.txt, so nothing else needs
# to reach the daemon - but this is written as a denylist of the known-big
# irrelevant stuff, NOT an "exclude everything, then negate" allowlist.
# The allowlist form (`*` + `!cwatm/` + ...) built cleanly with local
# BuildKit but failed on the Accelerator's buildah-based build server with
# "no items matching glob .../requirements_docker.txt" - a top-level file
# right next to the Dockerfile, so the repo clone was fine and this was a
# buildah .dockerignore negation bug, not a missing file. A denylist has
# nothing to negate, so it can't hit that class of bug; the whole repo
# (tauri-app aside, which doesn't exist on this branch) is only ~50MB
# anyway, so being generous here costs nothing.
.git/
tauri-app/
documentation/
assets/
supabase/
tests/
gamification/
installer/
translations/
tools/
.github/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
